  "placementEffectMinimalHelp": "With Minimal animations, placement feedback stays still.",
  "manualAssistanceBody": "Tap Circle on your side of the board, or Hint on Play, for a suggested move. Litch prepares a Hint as your turn begins and can refine it while you wait. While you hold the suggested piece, its Hint destination stays stable; lifting another piece shows that piece’s normal legal moves.\n\nOn Play, use Coaching’s P1 or P2 control to turn help on or off for that player, or hold their Circle button for about one second. Coaching shows help automatically on their human turns.",
  "manualAssistanceTitle": "Hints and Coaching",
  "manualComputerBody": "In Setup, choose the computer as your opponent, set its level, and choose which player it controls. The board chooses its moves; you move its pieces.\n\nWait for its source and destination lights, move the indicated chess piece, and remove any captured piece when prompted. Finish every lit step. In Duck, move the Duck to the computer’s indicated destination too.",
  "manualComputerTitle": "Play the computer",
  "manualControlsBody": "Each end has a four-direction D-pad, X, and Circle. In ordinary play, tap Circle for a Hint or X for Undo. Hold X for about one second to open Quick Setup. Left/Right chooses a setting, Up/Down changes it, and X closes the menu. On Bluetooth, move to another item before pressing X to close. Follow the lit controls when the board asks for a choice.\n\nIf the app says that Litch already has three saved Bluetooth devices, clear the board’s saved pairings to add another device.\n\nIf you control this board and it still will not connect, clear its saved phones. This removes all phones, tablets and other devices paired with this board. Your game and other settings stay intact. On that board in Play, hold X for about one second to open Quick Setup. Use Left or Right to select Bluetooth. At the same end, hold X and Circle together for two seconds. Release both buttons when the blue-and-orange animation starts, then wait for three success flashes. Return to Foxie Litch, choose your board and try connecting again in the app.\n\nIn Litchcraft, Left/Right opens the quick palette and Up/Down fine-adjusts the active colour. Tap X for Undo or Circle for Redo. Hold Circle for about one second to switch between Paint and Erase. Use the app to select, add, and play frames.\n\nHold X and Circle together at the same end for about 1.5 seconds, then release to exit Litchcraft. Both individual actions are consumed. Lift the brush and close the palette, then shake the board for about one second to clear the frame. Painting, reconnect, and exit must be finished first. Only the selected frame clears; Undo restores it. You can also shake your device with Litchcraft open to clear the selected frame.",
  "manualQuickSetupHeading": "Quick Setup on the board",
  "manualQuickCpuLevel": "Computer level",
  "manualQuickCpuPlayer": "Computer player",
  "manualQuickPlayerEnd": "Player 1 end",
  "manualQuickLightPreview": "The board previews the light squares directly.",
  "manualControlsTitle": "Board controls",
  "manualControlsRecovery": "Busy? Lift the brush or end the app stroke, then retry. Lifting alone never replays it.",
  "manualConnectionBody": "Keep the powered board nearby, enable Bluetooth on your device, and select your board in the app. Allow the requested permissions and follow the connection prompts.\n\nLitch connects to one device at a time. If another device is connected, open Litch on that device and tap Disconnect, then try again.\n\nIf connecting still fails, forget the correct Foxie Litch board in your phone’s Bluetooth settings. On iPhone or iPad: Settings → Bluetooth → ⓘ beside your board → Forget This Device. On Samsung: Settings → Connections → Bluetooth → gear beside your board → Unpair. On other Android phones, look under Connected devices or Bluetooth and choose Forget or Unpair for your board. If your board is not listed, continue with the board steps.\n\nIf you control this board and it still will not connect, clear its saved phones. This removes all phones, tablets and other devices paired with this board. Your game and other settings stay intact. On that board in Play, hold X for about one second to open Quick Setup. Use Left or Right to select Bluetooth. At the same end, hold X and Circle together for two seconds. Release both buttons when the blue-and-orange animation starts, then wait for three success flashes. Return to Foxie Litch, choose your board and try connecting again in the app.\n\nFollow any connection recovery shown in the app. For a power or sensor problem, follow the Board health instructions. Use Contact Support in Setup, or the discovery screen’s help option if your board cannot connect. You can review and edit a report before opening an email draft.\n\nIf your board runs custom firmware, it must support the Litch connection protocol to work with the app. Use USB to restore the official firmware, or open Contact Support for help.\n\nWhen newer board software is available, the app shows its release notes once for each version after connecting. Choose Later to continue, or Review update to open Board update. Review the notes there and choose Update Board when you are ready; opening the page never installs an update automatically. You can also open Board update from Setup or the Connected board menu.\n\nThe app shows its release notes once after an update. It does not appear on a first install. The app notes and board update offers have independent checkboxes for hiding future notices. You can still open Board update at any time.",
  "manualConnectionTitle": "Connect and get help",
  "manualDescription": "Setup, play, and help. Available offline.",
  "manualDuckBody": "Before the first move, complete the normal 32-piece setup and add one extra piece on any of the four empty rows between the players’ pawns. Litch recognizes that piece as the Duck and marks it in yellow.\n\nEach turn has a chess move followed by moving the Duck to a different empty square. Finish both steps before the other player starts. With a hint, the lights guide your chess piece first. Once the board accepts that move, yellow lights show where to move the Duck. The Duck blocks squares and cannot be captured.\n\nThere is no check or checkmate. Capturing the opposing king wins immediately, without another Duck move. A player with no available chess move also wins.",
  "manualDuckTitle": "Duck chess",
  "manualIntroduction": "A practical guide to getting started and finding your next step on the board. No internet or board connection is needed to read it.",
  "manualSearchLabel": "Search the manual",
  "manualSearchNoResults": "No matching manual topics.",
  "manualMovesBody": "Lift a piece to see its legal destinations, then place it on a legal square. If Confirm moves is set to Confirm with Circle button, press Circle after placement. The move is accepted one second later. Timed confirmation happens automatically.\n\nRead a square by its file (a–h) and rank (1–8). Play and Game Review show these labels on all four edges. With White nearest you, a1 is at the lower left. When you swap player ends in Play or rotate the view in Game Review, h8 moves to the lower left. A move such as e2 to e4 still uses the same square names.\n\nFor a capture, remove the captured piece and place your piece on its destination. On supported boards, a bright amber pulse reminds you to remove the captured piece. With Minimal Animations, the reminder is steady orange. Castling also needs the rook move. Follow every lit step before the next turn. Promotion defaults to Queen, which is applied automatically after normal move confirmation. If Promotion is set to Choose, use Left/Right to choose a piece, then press Circle to confirm. If the board asks for correction, return the pieces to the indicated squares.",
  "manualMovesTitle": "Move the pieces",
  "manualLitchcraftBody": "Remove every piece from the board, then open Litchcraft beside Play—or hold X and Circle together for about 1.5 seconds at one end of an empty Setup board, then release. Litchcraft never interrupts a game in progress. You can create and save artwork in the app while the board is unavailable.\n\nChoose a colour and paint in the app, or touch empty board squares with a magnetic chess piece. Effects applies an effect to individual squares. The active tool tells you what the next square tap will do, even when another panel is open.\n\nOn a tablet in portrait, the tools sit below the canvas. A wide tray shows Colour and brushes together, LEDs and Effects in the middle, and Frames alongside them. In a narrower tray, select the section you want to use. In landscape, the tools sit beside the canvas. The arrow beside Rotate moves the tools and navigation to the other side. In a narrow landscape window, tap Show tools or Hide tools to open or close the panel.\n\nAnimation holds up to 256 frames. Tap a thumbnail to select it and pause playback. Add copies the selected frame. Hold a frame thumbnail, then confirm Delete, to remove it; at least one frame stays. Use Play/Pause for playback and the timing value for an exact duration.\n\nTap Fill to fill the selected frame with the active colour. Hold that same action for about half a second to clear the frame instead. Hold a colour swatch for half a second to fill the frame with that colour. Undo restores the edit.\n\nUse Artwork to save, import, or share. An editable artwork file keeps colours, effects, frames, and timing; an image is rendered artwork. Import previews conversion before you replace the current artwork. To leave the live board session, return to Play or use the board’s X-and-Circle chord.\n\nOn the board, tap X for Undo and Circle for Redo. Hold X for one second to erase the current frame; Undo restores it. Hold Circle for one second to switch Paint/Erase. The X+Circle exit gesture takes priority.",
  "manualLitchcraftTitle": "Paint with Litchcraft",
  "manualStartBody": "Keep the powered board nearby, enable Bluetooth on your device, and select your board in the app. Allow the requested permissions and follow the connection prompts. The list uses the board’s advertised name.\n\nWhen the app asks you to confirm a new pairing, press X and Circle together at either end of the board within ten seconds. After the board accepts, the app allows up to 40 seconds for the phone’s Pair prompt and the board to save the pairing. Keep the board powered and nearby until Connected appears.\n\nOn supported boards, Identify shows the board’s list number for about three seconds. Identify all does this for the listed boards in turn. The normal display returns automatically; no manual reconnect is needed. This temporary number is different from a paired board’s four-character ID. Compatible boards with firmware 1.0.4 report the same Bluetooth address ending on Android and iOS. If it is unavailable, no ID is shown.\n\nTap New game on Play, or hold X and Circle together at one end of the board for about two seconds.\n\nChoose Time limit on Play before starting. Use Setup to choose the first-player end, board rotation, and opponent. On the board, hold X for about one second to open Quick Setup.\n\nArrange the normal chess starting position and follow any placement lights. Arranging the pieces does not use clock time. The clock starts when you lift the first legal piece after the board is ready.",
  "manualStartTitle": "Start a game",
  "manualFactoryResetBody": "Factory reset permanently deletes board settings, saved-game data and all saved Bluetooth pairings. Your phone may still remember the board; forget that old pairing before pairing again. Try the recovery and Contact Support guidance first if you want to keep them.\n\nUnplug the board. Hold only Down at one end while reconnecting power. When the X and Circle lights blink amber, release Down and any other held controls. At the same end, hold X and Circle together for at least two seconds. Releasing either early cancels. If the hold is not completed within ten seconds of the amber prompt, the board boots normally.\n\nAfter a successful reset, the X and Circle lights blink green and the board restarts. Waking from sleep or restarting the board cannot start this reset. If reset fails, keep the board powered and use Contact Support.",
  "manualFactoryResetTitle": "Factory reset the board",
  "manualTitle": "Litch Manual",
  "manualUndoBody": "Tap X, or Undo on Play, then follow the return-square lights. Restore any captured piece when prompted. In Duck, a completed turn is undone by returning the Duck first, then the chess piece. On supported boards, unrelated squares dim while the piece to return and its return-square guidance stay bright.\n\nIf you undo a computer reply in Duck before lifting the Duck, first return the computer’s chess piece. Then follow the lights to return the Duck and your piece from the preceding turn.\n\nWhile Cancel Undo is available, select it to restore the forward move. If the Duck is in your hand, return it to its source before trying again. Finish all required returns before continuing play.",
  "manualUndoTitle": "Undo a move",
  "cpuIsThinking": "CPU is thinking",
  "cpuThinkingRemaining": "{seconds, plural, one{About {seconds} second left} other{About {seconds} seconds left}}",
  "automaticBrightness": "Automatic brightness",
  "automaticBrightnessHelp": "Disabled at level 0",
  "boardLightsManualLink": "How Board lights and animation work",
  "manualLightsBody": "Open Connected at the top of the app to control brightness and Automatic brightness. In Setup, Board lights and animation controls the light-square LEDs and other lighting behaviour. Automatic brightness is on by default. It blends the two light sensors to adjust the board to the room. Turn it off for a steady manual level; both sensors still take readings for diagnostics. Your choice is saved on the board.\n\nLevel 0 is near dark: essential cues stay dim and room light does not brighten them. Colour detail is reduced and dim background squares may disappear at this level. With Automatic brightness off, level 8 requests the highest normal brightness. Power limits can reduce the actual output.\n\nWith Automatic brightness on, the slider sets the maximum; the lights dim below it in darker rooms. Turning Auto off uses the same saved level as steady manual brightness.",
