  "aboutOpenSourceBody": "The mobile app is built with Flutter, Reactive BLE, and other open-source projects.",
  "aboutThanksBody": "Foxie Litch was designed by Will Fox and Brandon Anderson, with thanks to every maker, player, tester, teacher, and friend who helped make it real. You all are the real Litches we met along the way.",
  "aboutLicenseNotice": "Software licenses and notices for the app and board firmware.",
  "manualClockTitle": "Game clock",
  "manualClockBody": "Choose Time limit on Play before the first legal pickup. Each player gets their own time. 3+2 means three minutes each, plus two seconds after each completed turn. 15+10 means fifteen minutes each, plus ten seconds per turn. The compact board menu shows only the starting minutes. Choose No clock to play without a time limit.\n\nArranging the pieces uses no time. Once the board is ready, the clock starts at the first legal pickup. Putting that piece back does not refill the clock or let you change the preset; start a new game to change it.\n\nOpening Quick Setup on the board pauses the clock. It resumes with the same remaining time when you close the menu or it closes after ten idle seconds. Browsing app pages or settings does not pause it. Correction and uncertain board input pause play; keep the pieces still and follow the next-action guidance.\n\nIn Duck, the chess move and Duck relocation are one timed turn. Your time keeps running until both finish, then the clock switches and adds the increment once. Capturing the opposing king ends the game immediately. When playing the computer, its thinking time counts; both clocks pause while you carry out its chosen move. This clock is a casual play aid.",
  "manualRecoveryTitle": "Board health and recovery",
  "manualRecoveryBody": "Open Board health in Setup when the board needs attention. Healthy means the board reports normal sensor and power status. A usable warning lets play continue, sometimes with reduced brightness. Follow the message for the next step; reconnecting alone does not clear a power warning.\n\nIf board input is paused, input and clocks wait while the board checks its sensors. Keep the pieces still. After recovery, follow any placement correction before continuing.\n\nA storage warning means current changes may not survive power-off. Keep the board powered, save app artwork to your library, and open Contact Support if the warning remains. Do not assume a reconnect or a restart saved the changes.\n\nIf startup stops in recovery, hold Circle alone at one end for about 1.5 seconds to retry without deleting settings or saved games. Release early to cancel. If retry does not help, use Contact Support. A recovery reset permanently deletes board settings and saved-game data: hold X and Circle at the same end for about five seconds, then through the final two-second keep-held signal. Releasing either button cancels. Use this only when you intend to reset; waiting never deletes data. A recovery reset also clears all saved Bluetooth pairings.",
